  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "mrb_str_concat",
    "file": "mruby/src/string.c",
    "description": "`mrb_str_concat` forwards `self` directly to `mrb_str_cat_str` without validating that `self` is actually a String. In the OP_STRCAT VM path (`mrb_vm_exec`), fuzzed bytecode/state can make `regs[a]` non-string; `mrb_str_cat` then does `mrb_str_ptr(str)` and later `mrb_str_modify`/`mrb_check_frozen` on an invalid pointer, causing the wild read crash in `mrb_check_frozen`. Root cause is missing type check/sanitization of concat receiver before string internals are accessed.",
    "conditions": "Input is Ruby source fed by `mruby_fuzzer` (`mrb_load_string`) that compiles to code executing `OP_STRCAT` with a non-String destination register value (`regs[a]`). When `mrb_vm_exec` executes `mrb_str_concat(mrb, regs[a], regs[a+1])`, `other` is coerced to string but `self` is not checked, so invalid object type reaches `mrb_str_cat` and crashes during frozen check on bogus `RString*`."
  },
